      "writtenOn": "2022-04-12T23:14:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The mux nodes don\u0027t need to live under a separate parent.  I think I prefer the mux nodes to be nested under the USB-C port.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "70428f74ff452d2b57c81e867c673a97990d3708",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fdb02cab_6440ceff",
        "filename": "zephyr/projects/corsola/usbc_krabby.dts",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1511343
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-13T19:09:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It cannot be done this way, because Zephyr doesn\u0027t allow circular dependencies in DTS (e.g. it5205 depends on port, because it is child node and port depends on it5205, because of phandle in usb-muxes property).\n\nI see here 2 options:\n1) Keep it as it is: usb-muxes is property of named-usbc-port and USBC muxes nodes are not descendants of named-usbc-port.\n2) Make USBC muxes nodes children of named-usbc-port and move usb-muxes property to node that is sibling of USBC muxes or named-usbc-port.",
      "parentUuid": "3d6c7974_70d259d4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "70428f74ff452d2b57c81e867c673a97990d3708",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
